  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-Sectoral Humanitarian Assistance for Displaced and Mobile Populations in Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sudan remains one of the world&#x2019;s largest protracted humanitarian crises with needs increasingly more complex, despite the appointment of a transitional government in August 2019. Continuing economic challenges (characterized by high inflation, unstable markets, and fuel and cash shortages), political upheaval and transition, localized instability, and on-going protracted displacement, are expected to increase fragility and insecurity and vulnerabilities over the upcoming year &#x2013; exacerbated by the ongoing COVID-19 pandemic. The project aims to address critical humanitarian needs through a multi-sectoral approach to provide integrated support to displaced and vulnerable crisis-affected populations. The project will focus on: (1) collecting and sharing up-to-date information with partners in order to respond effectively to humanitarian needs through the Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM); (2) providing life-saving assistance to crisis-affected populations to reduce their vulnerability, restore a minimum sense of dignity, mitigate health risks, and improve living conditions including shelter and non-food items and cash-based assistance to meet basic needs for food and other items; and (3) reducing risks of fragility and vulnerability through improving access to basic services including water sanitation and hygiene (WASH), health and nutrition services, and livelihood opportunities to generate incomes and address food insecurity and malnutrition.</narrative>
  </description>
